from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
load=lambda n:json.loads((R/n).read_text(encoding='utf8'))
c=load('PROSE-COUNTS.json')['main'];g=load('R2-SLOT9-GEOMETRY.json')
names={'paragraph_first':'Paragraph-first word','continuation_first':'Continuation-line first word','opening_line_other':'Other words in paragraph-first line','continuation_other':'Other words in continuation lines'}
lines=['f57v slot 9 and prose f/p: retrospective boundary-transfer audit, v102',
'Result: shared paragraph-opening preference in prose; the proposed immediate-boundary transfer to f57v is not supported.',
'',
'GEOMETRY',
'The 159 v39 image regions register R3/R4, not R2. Slot 9 belongs to R2. The corrected v39 R4 origin concerns another ring and cannot define the R2 start.',
'v31 explicitly assigns R2 no independent cut. Four v37 anchor rays are defined by the recurring o signs; these are analytical rays, not registered physical dividers. No fitted physical spoke-crossing ledger exists for R2 in these sources.',
'New inspection of the original full page and native-resolution polar strips shows no radial divider or spoke crossing immediately before/through any of the four slot-9 signs. Slot 9 is inside each run, eight transcribed units after its o, preceded by k then k/m, followed by &169. The plumed sign is not the first sign after the o-defined run boundary.',
'Other-ring local NW cuts are ring-specific: R1 about 10:30, R3 10:00-10:30, R4 9:30-10:00. Their projection into R2 would be a new assumption. No visible same-ring break distinguishes f/f from p/p.',
'Angles below are approximate manual ink neighborhoods in the existing polar coordinate system, rounded to degrees; added neighborhood uncertainty is 20 strip pixels, about 1.5 degrees, plus unquantified center/anchor error. Not statistical confidence intervals.']
for x in g:lines.append(f"Cycle {x['cycle']}: {x['reading']['H']}; approximately {x['angle_clockwise_north_nominal']:.0f} degrees clockwise from north, {x['degrees_after_own_o_ray_nominal']:.0f} degrees after own o ray. Interior slot; no independent R2 cut assigned.")
lines += ['', 'PROSE',
'Word-initial EVA f and p, strict readable original slots in P loci. Paragraph status from explicit source line 1 / preceding =; continuation after - in the same source series. Unknown or comma-marked slots are not promoted. Main excludes lines with fewer than two original slots. H/F are alternate readings, not independent replications.',
'Position | H f | H p | F f | F p']
for k,label in names.items():
 vals=[]
 for tr in ['H','F']:
  d=c[tr][k];n=d['opportunities']
  for ch in ['f','p']:vals.append(f"{d[ch]['initial']}/{n} ({d[ch]['initial_rate']*100:.2f}%)")
 lines.append(label+' | '+' | '.join(vals))
lines += [
'Both signs concentrate in paragraph-first lines. f is not a generic continuation-line initial: H has only 2 and F only 1. p strongly favors the first word itself. H f anywhere within a word: paragraph-first word 38/689 (5.52%), other opening-line words 275/5834 (4.71%); p 341/689 (49.49%) versus 811/5834 (13.90%). Thus word initials and presence anywhere in the line are distinct effects; cfh/cph compound occurrences are separately counted in the JSON.',
'Among f/p-initial words H p-share is 91.3% at paragraph-first word, 95.2% at continuation-line first word, 67.5% elsewhere on opening lines, 64.9% elsewhere on continuation lines. F: 91.6%, 97.4%, 67.4%, 76.2%. These do not show f replacing p at ordinary line starts; both are rare there.',
'Within identical remaining word body, hand, Currier, section and original train/test allocation: paragraph-first versus other opening-line words has only 6 informative H cells (5 favor p at first, 1 reverse), 9 F cells (8 favor p, 1 reverse). Matched counts: H first p/f=11/1 versus other=16/8; F 14/1 versus 15/10. H reverse body olaiin; F reverse body cheo, retained. Paragraph-first versus continuation-first has ZERO informative matched cells. Continuation-first versus other continuation words has only ONE informative cell each. No fitted/predictive f/p alternation rule is qualified.',
'The all-line-length and shared-H/F-structure sensitivities retain the broad pattern; every stratum, zero cell and token event is saved. Hand/section/Currier and reused train/test counts are descriptive, not new heldout validation.',
'', 'ORIGINAL p/r RECEIPT',
'Saved predictions reproduce exactly p=12/12 at line-first versus 9/45 elsewhere among the selected p/r word variants. This is not an all-token p rate. The 12 line-first events decompose into 8 paragraph-first and 4 continuation-first. Of the other 45, all 9 p events occur elsewhere in paragraph-first lines; 8 r there, 27 r in continuation interiors, and 1 r is excluded by the stricter current structural/reading filter.',
'', 'INTERPRETATION',
'The prose family resemblance is supported descriptively: both f/p favor opening lines, with p stronger at the initial word. The proposed ring-segment-start explanation has no observed structural boundary at slot9 and no boundary change across its four copies. This does not exclude a nonlocal, unmarked or procedural relationship; none is demonstrated here. No meanings, sounds, interchangeable-sign equivalence, causal mechanism or out-of-sample cross-format prediction follows.',
'', 'RECEIPTS',
'Run python audit.py then python publish.py from this folder (or use absolute script paths). Inputs are absolute paths in INPUT-FREEZE.json. Geometry, all prose events, strata, matched cells, failed support and sensitivities are saved separately. Input hashes verified unchanged; old experiments untouched. Image boxes are new provisional manual annotations, not expert adjudication.'
]
(R/'REPORT.txt').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
rows=''.join('<tr><td>'+html.escape(names[k])+'</td>'+''.join(f"<td>{c[t][k][ch]['initial']}/{c[t][k]['opportunities']}<small>{c[t][k][ch]['initial_rate']*100:.2f}%</small></td>" for t in ['H','F'] for ch in ['f','p'])+'</tr>' for k in names)
geom=''.join(f"<tr><td>{x['cycle']}</td><td><b>{x['reading']['H']}</b></td><td>{x['angle_clockwise_north_nominal']:.0f}°</td><td>{x['degrees_after_own_o_ray_nominal']:.0f}°</td><td>Interior; no independent R2 cut</td></tr>" for x in g)
paras=''.join('<p>'+html.escape(s)+'</p>' for s in lines[lines.index('Both signs concentrate in paragraph-first lines. f is not a generic continuation-line initial: H has only 2 and F only 1. p strongly favors the first word itself. H f anywhere within a word: paragraph-first word 38/689 (5.52%), other opening-line words 275/5834 (4.71%); p 341/689 (49.49%) versus 811/5834 (13.90%). Thus word initials and presence anywhere in the line are distinct effects; cfh/cph compound occurrences are separately counted in the JSON.'):])
doc='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>f57v slot 9 · f/p boundary audit</title><style>body{max-width:1120px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 24px;font:17px/1.65 system-ui;color:#203432;background:#f8f5ed}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.14}h2{margin-top:42px}p{max-width:960px}.eyebrow{color:#176d66;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:13px}.finding{padding:20px 25px;background:#dcebe3;border-left:5px solid #176d66}img{width:100%;border:1px solid #d5d5c7}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:20px 0}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #d3d8cc}small{display:block;color:#526c67}a{color:#176d66}.caption{font-size:14px;color:#526c67}</style><div class="eyebrow">V102 · RETROSPECTIVE AUDIT · NO SEMANTIC CLAIM</div><h1>Shared opening preference.<br>No observed ring-start transfer.</h1><p class="finding">f shares p’s paragraph-opening preference in prose. But f57v’s f/f/p/p copies all occupy the same interior slot, without a visible local divider separating the two forms.</p><h2>Where slot 9 sits</h2><p>v39’s 159 registrations cover R3/R4. The repeated sequence is R2. v31 assigns R2 no independent cut. The blue rays below mark recurring o signs, not physical dividers; the red boxes mark newly inspected, approximate slot-9 neighborhoods.</p><img src="R2-slot9-comparison.png" alt="Four R2 strips showing slot9 f f p p inside uninterrupted runs"><p class="caption">Existing 4800-pixel polar transform; unequal real spacing preserved. Slot 9 is eight units after its o anchor, with seven intervening signs. Boxes are provisional manual neighborhoods.</p><table><tr><th>Cycle</th><th>H/U/V</th><th>From north</th><th>After own o</th><th>Boundary assessment</th></tr>'''+geom+'''</table><p>Angles are rounded, approximate image positions. No fitted R2 spoke-crossing record exists in the prior ledgers. Neighboring-ring NW cuts do not establish a divider in R2.</p><h2>The prose companion</h2><p>Word-initial f/p counts; denominators are readable original word slots. Paragraph and continuation starts remain separate. H and F are dependent alternate readings.</p><table><tr><th>Position</th><th>H f</th><th>H p</th><th>F f</th><th>F p</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table>'''+paras+'''<p><a href="REPORT.txt">Full plain-text report</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a> · <a href="PROSE-COUNTS.json">Counts and sensitivities</a> · <a href="MATCHED-FP-CELLS.json">All matched cells</a> · <a href="R2-SLOT9-GEOMETRY.json">Geometry</a> · <a href="INPUT-FREEZE.json">Input hashes</a></p>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(doc,encoding='utf8')
assert all(hashlib.sha256(Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==v for p,v in load('INPUT-FREEZE.json').items())
(R/'SHA256SUMS.json').write_text(json.dumps({p.name:hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in R.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name!='SHA256SUMS.json'},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
print('Published REPORT.txt and report.html; input hashes unchanged.')
